From d246c5c77e8c06604dd3dab9228e698bb4c9cbb1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Daniel Campos Ramos <Capitain_Jack@yahoo.com>
Date: Mon, 5 Oct 2026 22:57:24 -0300
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] Show a 3D video to the compositor as stereo content

Under a compositor that takes stereo content declarations (kde_stereo_content_v1,
with wl_subcompositor, wp_viewporter and wl_shm), the video of a stereoscopic 3D
file, whatever its packing, is drawn into a surface of its own under the window's
surface: both views side by side at the size of one view, the left eye first, and
declared as full side by side. The controls stay in the window's surface over it,
the same in both eyes, and what the layer does not cover is black. Qt creates
subsurfaces only above their parent, so the layer is a wl_subsurface made here.
The StereoFilter hands the layer the two views of every frame; the frames of a
frame sequence are shown as a pair when the second one has come.

The 3D Video menu gets a 3D entry (the default where the layer is supported) and
Display Settings, which opens the screen's settings where its 3D mode is chosen.
Dragon Player never outputs another packing: that is what the output filters of
the display part are for. Anaglyph videos are shown as they are. Everywhere else
Dragon Player works as before.

Assisted-by: Claude Sonnet via Claude Code
